<title>SINGAPORE: Lum Chang completes Solarvest stake sale.</title>
<headline>Lum Chang completes Solarvest stake sale.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lum Chang Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday it had completed the divestment of a 67.0 million ringgit interest in Malaysia's Solarvest Sdh Bhd owned through two subsidiary companies.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement its units Lum Chang (M) Sdn Bhd and LC Development Ltd had each sold stakes of 33.5 million ringgit in Solarvest to a wholly-owned subsidiary of Sime Darby Bhd.</p>
<p>The statement said the sale would realise extraordinary gains of Singapore $18.0 million and S$17.0 million for Lum Chang and LC Development respectively for the year to June 30 1997.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
